-- title:
--   Stalks at the two special-fibre generic points have dimension one
-- statement:
--   Let $p$ be a prime and let $\mathfrak{X}$ be a `DRModelPackage p`, i.e. a bundle of data and properties for the two-chart integral model `DRModel p` over $\mathbb{Z}$ (the pushout of the two affine charts attached to the full modular function field in level $p$ and its Igusa $j$-invariant), comprising properness, flatness and integrality of `DRModel.toBase p`, normality on affine opens, rational and geometric curve models with their Galois compatibilities, two sections over $\operatorname{Spec}\mathbb{Z}$, a smooth locus, and further fields. Let $O$ be a discrete valuation ring (a domain) whose maximal ideal is the principal ideal generated by the image of $p$, let $\kappa$ be an algebraically closed field of characteristic $p$, and let $\mathrm{to}\kappa : O \to \kappa$ be a ring homomorphism (no compatibility with the valuation is assumed). Write $X_O$ for the fibre product of `DRModel.toBase p` with $\operatorname{Spec}(\mathbb{Z}\to O)$, and `DRModel.baseChangeMap toκ` for the induced morphism from the analogous fibre product over $\kappa$ to $X_O$, obtained from $\operatorname{Spec}$ of $\mathrm{to}\kappa$ on the base. Then for each of the two morphisms $\mathfrak{X}.\mathrm{compInf}\,\kappa$ and $\mathfrak{X}.\mathrm{compZero}\,\kappa$ from the scheme underlying $\mathfrak{X}.\mathrm{ratModel}\,\kappa$ into the fibre product over $\kappa$, the image of the generic point of that scheme under the given morphism followed by `DRModel.baseChangeMap toκ` is a point of $X_O$ whose local ring has Krull dimension exactly $1$.
--
--   This is the statement that the two components of the special fibre of the Deligne–Rapoport integral model, base changed to a discrete valuation ring with uniformiser $p$, have one-dimensional local rings at their generic points, i.e. that these points are codimension-one points of $X_O$. It is used in the analysis of the points of $X_O$ lying over the closed point of $\operatorname{Spec} O$, via [`ModularCurve.DRModelPackage.isClosed_or_eq_generic_of_snd_eq_closedPoint`](thm.html#ModularCurve.DRModelPackage.isClosed_or_eq_generic_of_snd_eq_closedPoint).
